          "source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/RobertAHeinlein_ForUsTheLiving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=original",
          "width": 254,
          "height": 390
        },
        "pageimage": "RobertAHeinlein_ForUsTheLiving.jpg",
        "extract": "For Us, the Living: A Comedy of Customs is a science fiction novel by American writer Robert A. Heinlein.  It was written in 1938 and published for the first time in 2003.  Heinlein admirer and science fiction author Spider Robinson titled his introductory essay \"RAH DNA\", as he believes this first, unpublished novel formed the DNA of Heinlein's later works.\nThe novel's manuscript was lost until biographer Robert James traced down references to it.  His research led to its rediscovery in a box left in a garage.  Heinlein had apparently sent it to an earlier biographer, Leon Stover.",
        "pageprops": {
          "defaultsort": "For Us, The Living: A Comedy Of Customs",
